==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]], Angel Fanboy was the only enemy whose trait was not mentioned in the [[Enemy Guide]], as traits used to be listed next to enemy names rather than in the upper-right corner of the Enemy Guide.
**The reason behind his bizarre attributes is to prevent him from being killed in one hit before the player has the chance to read his sign, while not encouraging the player to bring an [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal unit]] for such a trivial enemy.
*Prior to [[Version 6.4 Update|Version 6.4]], which added [[Grotesque Gallery]], Angel Fanboy was exclusively found in Event Stages.
*When [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] were first introduced to [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], they were not targeted by the abilities of "anti-all" units such as [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], encouraging use of dedicated [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel units]]. Though quickly changed, this was deliberate, as Angel Fanboy's Japanese description used to say that special abilities other than anti-Angel abilities would not work. Even after the anti-all units were updated to target Angels, Angel Fanboy's descriptions remained the same until [[Version 6.6 Update|Version 6.6]], which added [[Youcan]], an Angel/Alien hybrid enemy who is also vulnerable to [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien abilities]].
**His English description used to say "Angels can't be hurt by non-Angelic attacks" instead of "Angels aren't actually [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating enemies]]".
**His Japanese description used to say "天使には、天使属性以外の特殊攻撃が効かない" ("Angels aren't affected by special attacks, except for anti-Angel ones") instead of "天使には、浮いてる敵属性の特殊攻撃が効かない ("Angels aren't affected by anti-Floating special attacks").
*Prior to Version 6.6, Angel Fanboy's sign said "Anti-Floating type enemies!!" rather than "Anti-Floating attacks!".
*The line "invested all of his wealth because of an Angel" in his Japanese description could be a joke playing off of the term "angel investor".
*His advice is actually incorrect in the case of one enemy: [[Bears Be Back]] defy the rule by having both Floating and Angel traits among many others.
*In other languages that can be selected in [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]], such as Spanish and French, the text on this enemy's sign is still in English. Angel Fanboy shares this particularity with [[Ms. Sign]], but not [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]], as Aku Researcher's sign is actually translated across all languages.
*Angel Fanboy, [[Ghost Doge]], [[Ghost Snache]], [[Ghost Baa Baa]] and [[Idi:Re]] are the only enemies in [[Stories of Legend]] that do not appear in [[Uncanny Legends]].
**Idi:Re is the only one that was not introduced in an event stage.
*Interestingly enough, unlike [[Ms. Sign]]'s sign which switches to English in [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], Angel Fanboy's sign remains with Japanese text on and does not translate to English when switching the console's settings to English.
**This was later fixed in the [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.9 Update|Patch 1.0.9 Update]] as he now carries his sign in English.

